---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ScreenshotSlot from '../../components/ScreenshotSlot.astro';
import TransportPlanner from '../../components/TransportPlanner.astro';
import WorkshopLinks from '../../components/WorkshopLinks.astro';
import art from '../../assets/projects/transport.png';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<SiteLayout title="Automated Public Transport Planning" description="A Cities: Skylines 1 mod that will plan bus lines from your city's demand. Early preview 0.2.0 surveys your network and offers read-only diagnostics." path="automated-public-transport-planning/" active="mods">
	<section class="hero page-wrap">
		<div class="hero-copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Mod 02 · Early preview 0.2.0</p>
			<h1>Automated Public Transport Planning</h1>
			<p class="hero-lead">Planning a good bus network means studying where people live, work and travel. This mod will do that planning for you: it will propose bus lines from real demand, preview each one, and build nothing until you accept it.</p>
			<div class="status-strip"><span class="tag">Read-only: never changes your save</span><span class="tag">Route planning in development</span><span class="tag">11 languages</span></div>
			<WorkshopLinks mod="transport" />
		</div>
		<figure class="hero-art"><Image src={art} alt="Automated Public Transport Planning artwork" widths={[560, 720]} sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 45vw" format="webp" quality={78} loading="eager" /><figcaption class="art-note">Project artwork · not a gameplay screenshot</figcaption></figure>
	</section>

	<nav class="subnav page-wrap" aria-label="Transport planning guide"><a href={base + 'wiki/transport/overview/'}>Guide</a><a href={base + 'wiki/project/roadmap/'}>Roadmap</a></nav>

	<section class="section soft">
		<div class="page-wrap columns">
			<div class="text-stack">
				<p class="eyebrow">In this preview</p>
				<h2>Survey first. Plan later.</h2>
				<p>When a city loads, the mod quietly surveys its roads, stops and transit network. Nothing is created, changed or removed. The mod options add a Diagnostics group whose results are written to the game log:</p>
				<ul class="feature-list">
					<li><strong>Measure planning costs</strong><span>How long planning work would take on your city (a brief pause).</span></li>
					<li><strong>Capture a world snapshot</strong><span>A summary of the roads and stops the planner would use.</span></li>
					<li><strong>Build the route graph</strong><span>The network of possible stop connections.</span></li>
				</ul>
				<p>Testing this preview on real cities of every size helps shape the planner before it arrives.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="screenshot-stack">
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Diagnostics in the mod options" description="The language selector and the Diagnostics buttons on the mod’s options page." />
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Survey results in the log" description="The summary written to the game log after a city loads or a diagnostic runs." />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="interactive-section"><div class="page-wrap"><p class="section-label">Coming next · how planning will work</p><h2>From demand to a bus line you approve.</h2><TransportPlanner locale="en" /></div></section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="page-wrap columns">
			<div class="text-stack"><p class="eyebrow">Roadmap</p><h2>One step at a time.</h2><p>Each step ships only when it is safe for your save. Line creation will always wait for your confirmation.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + 'wiki/project/roadmap/'}>Full roadmap →</a></div>
			<div class="roadmap"><article><strong>Now · 0.2.0</strong><p>Read-only network survey and diagnostics.</p></article><article><strong>Next</strong><p>Demand analysis and candidate stops for a proposed line.</p></article><article><strong>Then</strong><p>Line previews you review and accept before anything is built.</p></article></div>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
